-- title:
--   Sections through a crossing: first reduction and non-strictness
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a positive integer with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ contain every unit reducing to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, and assume $j$, as a $q$-expansion, lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model datum `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, with algebraically closed residue field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R_p \to A$ compatible with $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $pb$ be a unit of $\mathbb{Z}/(M/p)$ represented by $p$, and let $\delta$ act on places of $\mathrm{Fbar} =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC κ (ΓN p M H hpM)` through the diamond automorphism attached to a $\Gamma_0(M/p)$-lift of $pb$. Let $SS$ be a finset of pairs of places whose members are exactly the pairs $(\mathrm{Frob}\,v, v)$ with $v$ supersingular. Further data: an automorphism $\theta$ of $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,M\,H$ realised geometrically by $\mathfrak{X}.w$ on generic points (hypothesis `hwgen`), an integral algebra map $\alpha$ from level $M/p$ with $\theta \circ \alpha$ integral and $\alpha$ the identity on underlying Laurent series, a place specialisation $Psp$ with prolongation datum $Rpd$ satisfying the type dichotomy and the model laws for $\alpha$, $\theta\circ\alpha$, $\delta$, and the two compatibility tables `hcompat`, `hcompat'` expressing the places of closed points on the two components of the geometric special fibre in terms of `reduceFst`, `reduceSnd` and the mod-$p$ Frobenius on places (summarised here). Finally let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\rho_O : R_p \to O$, maximal ideal generated by $p$, a surjection $toκ : O \to \kappa$ over $\rho$, and $jO : O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $\iota_A : O \to A$ compatible with $\rho_O$, $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $toκ$; let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two components, $U$ an open of $XO = \mathfrak{X} \times_{R_p} \mathrm{Spec}\,O$ containing the image $x_n$ of $n$, $nd \in SS$ the node pair of $n$ (i.e. $(\mathfrak{X}.placeOn0\,n, \mathfrak{X}.placeOn1\,n) = nd$), and $W$ a place of $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,M\,H$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Write $prJ$ for the map from the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-fibre to $XO$ induced by $jO$. Then there is a morphism $s : \mathrm{Spec}\,A \to U$ which is a section over $O$ along $\iota_A$, whose generic point is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $W$ transported by $\mathfrak{X}.eeta$ and $prJ$, and whose closed point maps to $x_n$, if and only if $Psp.reduceFst\,\alpha\,W$ equals the first place of $nd$ and $W$ is strict of neither the first nor the second kind.
--
--   This is the domain clause in the analysis of the annulus attached to a supersingular crossing of a Deligne–Rapoport model at $p$: it identifies exactly those geometric points of the generic fibre whose $A$-valued section specialises to a given crossing, in terms of the reduction of the corresponding place to level $M/p$ and the failure of strictness on either branch. It is used in the subsequent construction of the crossing annuli and of the slope data attached to them.
